title: AlcoveScript
---
Narrator:Crashing waves echo off the cave walls, a constant ringing sound that never fully deserts the space.
Narrator:The sun bathes the walls in honeyed rays that gently heat them like palming a mug of warmed tea.
Narrator:Dampened sand coats each splayed digit of Nisaea's fresh, human toes as she carefully scales the alcove's outside wall.
Narrator:Dipping inside quickly to ensure that no one sees her, Nisaea lets out a loud groan.
<<reveal_object "Nisaea-FullBody">>
Nisaea:"My precious time was wasted on command. I ought to be with my pod, hunting, rendering myself useful."
Nisaea:"I would rather watch pups or feed elders than suffer what turned out to be a trivial errand." 
Nisaea:"I'll return with a few more fish than we had, so I suppose what reason have I to cavil?"
Narrator:Nisaea looped the string of fish she had bartered for around her waist and began looking in the sand for her pelt.
<<hide_object "Nisaea-FullBody">>
===
title: footprint_clue
---
<<reveal_object "Nisaea-FullBody">>
<<expression Nisaea Nervous>>
Narrator:A footprint larger than her own is preserved in the damp sand near the alcove mouth edge.
Narrator:It looks as if someone tried to disturb the print, but was in a hurry and could not destroy it.
Narrator:Upon closer inspection, the print is a shoe print. A print large enough Nisaea that can fit her entire human foot inside.
Nisaea: <i>Who would wear their boots upon the strand?</i>
<<hide_object "Nisaea-FullBody">>
===
title: overturnedrock_clue
---
<<reveal_object "Nisaea-FullBody">>
<<expression Nisaea Angry>>
Narrator:A large, smooth rock is sprayed wet with seawater.
Narrator:It is ashy and flaking with salt in the areas it has since dried off, and in the depressions brilliant pink coralline algae has made its home, making it difficult to grip from any angle.
Narrator:The rock seems to have been disturbed, with sand bunched up around its edges where it has been dragged from its original position.
Narrator:The pelt of Nisaea is missing from its hiding spot.
<<expression Nisaea Nervous>>
Narrator:Nisaea's heart began to race. She cannot differentiate between the sound of blood rushing through her ears and the waves creeping in to deposit sea foam on her feet.
Narrator:A guttural wail leaves her body, startling the gulls from their cozy perches.
Narrator:Nisaea is stranded. Without her pelt, she cannot return to her pod. She will never return home again.
Nisaea:"I exercised caution. I have obscured my passage. Who might have tracked me? Who desires to harm me?"
Narrator:Nisaea palmed the footprints and eyed the direction in which it was headed.
Nisaea:"It wends its way toward the town. Maybe I can find clues there."

<<change_scene TownSquare>>
===
